From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: size rotated planes' bandwidth by the rotated line width

_dpu_plane_calc_bw() estimates a pipe's fetch as src_width * vtotal *
fps * bpp. src_rect is kept in framebuffer orientation, so for a pipe
using 90/270 degree inline rotation each output line actually consumes
one source column: the per-line fetch is the source height, not its
width. On the AYN Odin 3 (1080x1920 panel, gamescope scanning out three
rotated 1920x1080 layers split across two mixers) this overestimates
each pipe by about 1920/540 = 3.6x; the display then holds a 6.5 GB/s
average DDR vote at idle and pins DDR at 1708 MHz.

Swap src_width/src_height for rotated pipes before the calculation. The
scale factor then also compares the rotated source height with the
destination height, as intended.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
@@ -128,6 +128,13 @@
 
 	src_width = drm_rect_width(&pipe_cfg->src_rect);
 	src_height = drm_rect_height(&pipe_cfg->src_rect);
+	/*
+	 * src_rect is in framebuffer orientation. With inline rotation each
+	 * output line consumes one source column, so the fetch per line is the
+	 * source height, not its width.
+	 */
+	if (pipe_cfg->rotation & DRM_MODE_ROTATE_90)
+		swap(src_width, src_height);
 	dst_height = drm_rect_height(&pipe_cfg->dst_rect);
 	fps = drm_mode_vrefresh(mode);
 	vbp = mode->vtotal - mode->vsync_end;
